Falsifies `page_frames::verification::mark_used_claims_exactly_the_frames_the_range_touches`.

The defect: `mark_used` rounds the end of the range down, `/` where the rule is `div_ceil`. It reads
as a harmless simplification of the arithmetic next to it, and it is exactly the rounding
`mark_free` needs, so the two functions look alike.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(fa.get(i), touched)`, on a range that ends mid-frame.
In the kernel that hands out the tail of the image, the frame its last byte shares with free memory.

diff --git a/crates/page_frames/src/lib.rs b/crates/page_frames/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/page_frames/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/page_frames/src/lib.rs
@@ -397,3 +397,3 @@
         let lo = (first / FRAME_SIZE) as usize;
-        let hi = (last.div_ceil(FRAME_SIZE) as usize).min(self.total);
+        let hi = ((last / FRAME_SIZE) as usize).min(self.total);
 
